  ],
  "description": "Series 80/80B four-band equalizer traced from Joel Cameron’s DIY Series 80-Type Equaliser, draft three (14 February 2008), cross-checked against the May 2008 S800 V2 board. Signal enters C4 after the line receiver and leaves the 50 Hz low-cut section before the balanced line driver. Both shelving controls share IC2. Both swept mid controls share IC3 and retain the interaction between the original bands. Each dual 100 kΩ reverse-log control tunes its TL071 active RC filter. Small-signal boost maxima span approximately 95–840 Hz and 0.98–14.1 kHz on this board. EQ bypass opens the shelf summing path and grounds the mid injection return. Source impedance is 47 Ω. R35 preserves the 15 kΩ load of the following balanced driver. Supply is ±18 V. Component values and lead designations refer to this documented S800 implementation.",
